#### Step 3: EKS Networking Fix

- **Egress Rules**:
  - Ensure your EKS pod’s security group allows outbound TCP `27017` to Atlas IPs (check Atlas "Network Access").
  - Test connectivity:
    ```bash
    kubectl exec -it <pod-name> -- telnet xxxxx.mongodb.net 27017
    ```

- **DNS**:
  - Verify SRV resolution:
    ```bash
    kubectl exec -it <pod-name> -- nslookup xxxxx.mongodb.net
    ```
  - Use explicit hosts if SRV fails:
    ```properties
    spring.data.mongodb.uri=mongodb://teamA_user:teamA_pass@cluster0-shard-00-00.abc123.mongodb.net:27017,cluster0-shard-00-01.abc123.mongodb.net:27017/teamA_db?retryWrites=true&w=majority
    ```

- **SSH Tunnel**:
  - Add a sidecar:
    ```yaml
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: app
        image: your-app-image:tag
        env:
        - name: SPRING_DATA_MONGODB_URI
          value: "mongodb://teamA_user:teamA_pass@localhost:27017/teamA_db?retryWrites=true&w=majority"
      - name: ssh-tunnel
        image: alpine:latest
        command: ["/bin/sh", "-c"]
        args:
        - "apk add openssh-client; ssh -L 27017:xxxxx.mongodb.net:27017 user@bastion-host -N"
    ```

